# Read by every bat invocation -- the `cat` alias, television and fzf previews,
# anything else that shells out to bat -- rather than only the alias, which is
# where these flags used to live.
#
# bat asks the terminal for its background and picks the matching theme, so
# output follows macOS light/dark in any terminal that answers. Coldark ships
# the pair.
--theme-dark="Coldark-Dark"
--theme-light="Coldark-Cold"
--italic-text=always
--style="numbers,changes,header"
